      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that you have extended the BackingObject type to add support for the restricted fd. A better approach might be to add a new field to MemoryRegion for the restricted fd instead. The main reason is that confidential computing proposals such as TDX and Arm CCA that encrypt the private memory, and therefore cannot do shared\u003c-\u003eprivate conversions in place, require two backing objects, one for the restricted/private memory, and another for the shared memory. The conversion happens by copying between the two. In the case of pKVM (and for Gunyah if I\u0027m not wrong) it\u0027s not the case, but crosvm should be able to support all cases. Moreover, I think that that would simplify the code a bit.\n\nFor reference, here\u0027s the proposed patch that adds TDX support to QEMU:\n\nhttps://github.com/chao-p/qemu/commit/7abaf69ea847e8bc1f57eeb907cf82d55b2ca271\n\nhttps://github.com/chao-p/qemu/blob/privmem-v10/include/exec/ramblock.h",
      "revId": "1a52951c0c11be0c810e181b70a0282506f8dab6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
